.TH NETWORK-INTERFACE-REPORT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
network-interface-report \- read-only network interface and IP address inventory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B network-interface-report
.RB [ --input " FILE|-]"]
.RB [ --format " auto|ip-json|ifconfig]"]
.RB [ --family " all|inet|inet6]"]
.RB [ --null ]
.br
.B network-interface-report
.RB [ --help " | " --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports interfaces, operating states, optional indices, IPv4/IPv6 addresses,
CIDR prefix lengths and Ethernet MAC addresses. No network configuration is
changed. A device can change while the native snapshot is collected.
.PP
Linux native backend uses
.B ip -j address show
and macOS/BSD native backend uses
.BR "ifconfig -a" .
Both executables are selected from fixed absolute paths and run without a
shell. Saved snapshots can be parsed offline on any supported Perl platform.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read a saved regular, non-symlink file or standard input. By default a
native backend is used.
.TP
.BI --format " auto|ip-json|ifconfig"
Select the snapshot parser; auto recognizes a JSON array or ifconfig text.
A forced native parser must agree with the native OS backend.
.TP
.BI --family " all|inet|inet6"
Select address families. Interfaces with no matching addresses remain in
output with FAMILY, ADDRESS and PREFIX set to a dash.
.TP
.B --null
Emit seven NUL-terminated fields per row without a header.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage information.
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version.
.SH OUTPUT
TSV columns, or corresponding NUL fields: INTERFACE, INDEX, STATE, FAMILY,
ADDRESS, PREFIX, MAC. INDEX is unavailable for ifconfig and shown as a dash.
IPv6 link-local scope identifiers are retained. IP and MAC fields are
sensitive inventory metadata.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Entire bounded snapshot parsed successfully.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or incompatible native format selection.
.TP
.B 3
Missing or failed backend, unsafe input file, malformed or oversized
snapshot. No partial report is printed.
.SH LIMITATIONS
At most 8 MiB of input, 512 interfaces, and 4,096 address records are
accepted. Optional ifconfig lines may be ignored. Native BSD execution has
not been validated by the M8.1 offline fixtures. An inventory is not a
reachability, routing, or intrusion assessment.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ip (8),
.BR ifconfig (8),
.BR tcp-check (1)
